Subject: fix: tick and cross on the Professor's "so your name is...?" question

The first Yes/No box of the game is made by the opening speech itself, not by the
field helper that draws the pictures, so it was the one box without them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CNqSDphYuD2Aqe9TExdQMP

diff --git a/src/oak_speech.c b/src/oak_speech.c
index e7741bafb..de4f25278 100644
--- a/src/oak_speech.c
+++ b/src/oak_speech.c
@@ -1499,6 +1499,8 @@ static void Task_OakSpeech_ConfirmName(u8 taskId)
             else
             {
                 CreateYesNoMenu(&sIntro_WindowTemplates[WIN_INTRO_YESNO], FONT_NORMAL, 0, 2, GetStdWindowBaseTileNum(), 14, 0);
+                // Little Trainers: the tick and the cross, as on every field Yes/No box
+                LT_DrawYesNoIcons(GetYesNoMenuWindowId(), 2, GetFontAttribute(FONT_NORMAL, FONTATTR_MAX_LETTER_HEIGHT) + GetFontAttribute(FONT_NORMAL, FONTATTR_LINE_SPACING));
                 gTasks[taskId].func = Task_OakSpeech_HandleConfirmNameInput;
             }
         }
